ct conclusion  to their story as a team the granddaddy  of the MCU Iron Man is just as good  today as it was in 2008 with heavy  hitters like the x-men and spider-man  already sold off to larger Studios  Marvel had to pull heroes from the bench  to launch its shared universe Iron Man  was one of the best of the rest so  director Jon Favreau was given a lot of  freedom and the studio banked on the  charisma of Robert Downey jr. the gamble  worked and this movie managed to tell an  extremely fun story while setting the  tone for a massive twenty billion dollar  franchise to follow it's also a textbook  example of how to get a superhero origin  story right I am Iron Man  over the course of 10 years and 18 films  Marvel had been preparing for the most  ambitious crossover event in movie  history  and when it came time for the world's  mightiest heroes to fight the universe's  biggest bad guy the results were better  than anyone could have dreamed 2018 s  infinity war quickly became one of the  highest-grossing films of all time  integrating countless characters into a  cohesive world most importantly infinity  war totally delivered when it came to  the mad Titan who Marvel fans had been  eagerly awaiting since 2012 in a  surprising twist Marvel even made Thanos  the film's true protagonist and then the  mad Titan wins the day and one of the  gutsiest  endings in blockbuster history watching  so many beloved characters turned to  dust is absolutely heartbreaking but it  also set the stage for the climactic  finale to Hollywood's most successful  franchise hi I'm Steve Rogers the  pinnacle of the MCU was established  relatively early on with a first ever  team up of Earth's Mightiest Heroes in  the Avengers written and directed by fan  favorite Joss Whedon the result proved  an unqualified critical and commercial  hit a new universe it's one of the most  successful films ever made  pulling in more than 1.5 billion dollars  worldwide and it scored some of the best  reviews