o a well-meaning  goofball I choose to run to warn my  problems and not away from them paired  with the nebbishy Bruce Banner Ragnarok  becomes an Odd Couple comedy and space  and the funniest film in the MCU add an  80s aesthetic the supercool score Thor  battling Hulk and a gladiator match and  a cast that includes Jeff Goldblum and  his strangest and all the problems out  of the Thor franchise are perfectly  hammered out the Winter Soldier is much  more than just the superhero movie it's  Marvel getting political Winter Soldier  finds her recently thought Steve Rogers  in a world where things aren't quite  black and white anymore it's hard to  know who to trust then cap quickly finds  himself in the middle of a conspiracy  that involves secret Hydra agents metal  armed assassins and worst of all an evil  Robert Redford with the fate of the  world hanging in the balance cap goes  rogue Winter Soldier features some of  the most suspenseful scenes you'll ever  see in a superhero film with tense  moments that boil over into fantastic  action scenes the film also shakes up  the MCU setting up the stakes for Civil  War Winter Soldier is a masterclass and  action intention and the best entry in  the Captain America franchise though the  big screen Superman is dark and dreary  these days he got his starts as a  brilliant red and blue beacon of hope  Richard Donner's 1978 Superman starring  Christopher Reeve was an instant classic  pulling in an a-list cast and telling a  classic story complete with a dastardly  Lex Luthor from the cutting-edge special  effects to the casting of the then  unknown Rivas Clark Kent superhero set  the template for the modern-day  superhero movies proving you could take  these characters seriously and still  have a whole lotta fun in the process  M night Shyamalan son breakable was a  brilliant exploration and deconstruction  of comic book characters at a time when  superhero movies weren't the juggernauts  of Hollywood they'd soon become and a  radical departure from the superhero  films that had come before  unbreakable treated superheroes  seriously laying the groundwork for many  comic-book movies to come plus the movie  just good Bruce Willis and samuel  l.jackson give outstanding performances  the score is incredibly haunting and the  film created a universe where James  McAvoy would someday unleash his inner  beast change was overdue in the MCU and  black panther pounced on to the scene  played by Chadwick Boseman T'Challa  first showed up in civil war and quickly  became a fan favorite the courageous cat  made his triumphant return in 2018 and  when his film hit theaters audiences  fell in love with what Conda  she never gets hard  [Music]  Black Panther is one of the  highest-grossing films of all time and  the first superhero movie to get an  Oscar nomination for Best Picture  talented actors like Lupita Nyong'o  Daniel Kuya and Angela Bassett struck a  chord with audiences and the African  setting allowed filmmaker Ryan Coogler  to explore a rich culture that's a  little seen in Hollywood films the film  also introduced one of the greatest bad  guys in superhero history Erick Gill  monger  played two villainous perfection by  Michael B Jordan kill monger is a stone  cold but sympathetic murderer with its  fantastic characters and beautiful world  building it's no wonder Black Panther  was a breakthrough hit the superhero  movie genre is mostly dominated by dudes  but the gender roles were finally  reversed in 2017 when the most iconic  female hero finally got her own movie  Wonder Woman was a critical success in a  box-office smash reinvigorating DC  superhero universe and giving kids a  different kind of hero to look up to in  a DC franchise that had up until then  been defined by grit and gloom this  Amazon princess emerged as a beacon of  courage and hope she isn't punching down  cities or branding bad guys  she's a protector of the people trying  to end all war unlike the DCE used  Batman or Superman  Diana actually cares about people and  sees the good in humanity she's more  concerned with saving lives than serving  justice Superman symbol might stand for  hope but it's Wonder Woman that restored  our faith and the power of superheroes  spider-man into the spider verse takes  the iconic web crawlers web slinging  mythos in exciting new directions by  introducing audiences to a vibrant world  of parallel dimensions parallel lives  and talking cartoon pigs you got a  problem with cartoon  the plot follows teenage Miles Morales  who's bitten by you guessed it's a  radioactive spider but things get even  more complicated when a powerful machine  opens up portals to other worlds  blasting a whole team's worth of  alternate universe spider people in two  miles as New York City  the film's brilliant animation captures  the feeling of reading in the comic  book-like view movies have before it it  couples the visuals with a daring story  that takes a daunting multiverse concept  and routes it in character moments that  any viewer can relate to young or old  most superhero movies are about special  people doing the impossible into the  spider versus a rare gem that makes you  feel like you can do the impossible -  2017 s Logan finally allowed Hugh  Jackman's Wolverine the r-rated chance  the slice and dices foes like Marvel's  own Freddy Krueger but the movie is so  much more than just an extra bloody  x-men adventure it's an ode to a hero at  the end of his life and a somber  meditation on violence regrets and  redemption inspired by classic westerns  in the old man Logan comic books  Logan stands apart from the rest of the  x-men series it takes the nearly  unkillable Wolverine and brings him back  down to earth as a broken forlorn mortal  man Jackman and co-star Patrick Stewart  gives some of the best performances of  their careers with stark portrayals of  their characters as dying men in a  defeated world their last mission is to  protect Laura a young clone of  Wolverines who still has hope for the  future the three leads surprisingly  familial connection makes a grounded and  emotional story that resonates in a way  few superhero movies can match that  happens to people I care about no sim  can obviously 2004's The Incredibles is  still one of the best superhero movies  and one of the best Pixar movies - it's  full of brilliant little moments that  stick in your memory like the hilarious  interviews that opened the film or the  macabre no capes montage there's also  the fact that this is a kids movie that  deals seriously with adult themes  characters go through midlife crises and  grapple with hiding their identities in  a world that won't accept them the  action sequences are fluid and fun just  as thrilling as almost anything you'll  see  a live-action Marvel or DC film but what  really elevates the movie is the family  at the center of the story who are  charming both at home and on the  battlefield they're also completely  believable as a family unit both of you  will get a grip or so help me I will  ground you for a month understand after  11 years and 21 films the Marvel  Cinematic Universe finally brought the  Infinity Saga to a close with endgame an  epic action flick that smashed  box-office records and said farewell to  some of our most beloved superheroes  despite running three hours long it  never feels its length with each act  feeling wildly different from the last  it all leads up to the most ambitious  superhero battle ever filmed featuring  dozens of characters from across the MCU  in a climactic battle for the fate of  the universe though it starts off with  the tone of mourning endgame ends up  feeling like an absolute joy its biggest  achievement is that it truly works as  the finale to a decade plus of  storytelling watching all of Marvel's  characters reunite one last time is  stirring  and while the MCU will likely continue  long past the original six Avengers  endgame provides the perfect conclusion  to their story as a team the granddaddy  of the MCU Iron Man is just as good  today as it was in 2008 with heavy  hitters like the x-men and spider-man  already sold off to larger Studios  Marvel had to pull heroes from the bench  to launch its shared universe Iron Man  was one of the best of the rest so  director Jon Favreau was given a lot of  freedom and the studio banked on the  charisma of Robert Downey jr. the gamble  worked and this movie managed to tell an  extremely fun story while setting the  tone for a massive twenty billion dollar  franchise to follow it's also a textbook  example of how to get a superhero origin  story right I am Iron Man  over the course of 10 years and 18 films  Marvel had been preparing for the most  ambitious crossover event in movie  history  and when it came time for the world's  mightiest heroes to fight the universe's  biggest bad guy the results were better  than anyone could have dreamed 2018 s  infinity war quickly became one of the  highest-grossing films of all time  integrating countless characters into a  cohesive world most importantly infinity  war totally delivered when it came to  the mad Titan who Marvel fans had been  eagerly awaiting since 2012 in a  surprising twist Marvel even made Thanos  the film's true protagonist and then the  mad Titan wins the day and one of the  gutsiest  endings in blockbuster history watching  so many beloved characters turned to  dust is absolutely heartbreaking but it  also set the stage for the climactic  finale to Hollywood's most successful  franchise hi I'm Steve Rogers the  pinnacle of the MCU was established  relatively early on with a first ever  team up of Earth's Mightiest Heroes in  the Avengers written and directed by fan  favorite Joss Whedon the result proved  an unqualified critical and commercial  hit a new universe it's one of the most  successful films ever made  pulling in more than 1.5 billion dollars  worldwide and it scored some of the best  reviews earned by any of the years wide  releases it's a comic book brought to  life in the best possible way and Whedon  managed to blend a bevy of characters  geek out fanservice and a compelling  story into one perfect package the  superhero movies genre was in its  infancy in 2004 but despite being  practically ancient spider-man 2 still  holds up this is a movie that features  an Evil Dead style horror sequence a  superhero showdown on a train the most  heartbreaking date ever filmed and a  villain who feels like an old-timey  Universal monster  none of this should fit together but it  all works perfectly  it does whatever a spider can means away  but spider-man 2 really shines by giving  us the most relatable superhero of all  time  unlike the mega-rich Batman or the  nearly immortal mutant Wolverine Peter  is just a normal guy trying to deliver  pizza and woo the girl of his dreams  while keeping the streets of New York  safe when he's not fighting  supervillains he's struggling with  everyday problems yeah he can shoot webs  and climb walls but this version of the  web crawler is still the most human  superhero we've ever seen the Dark  Knight isn't just the best superhero  movie ever made it assured in a new era  for comic book movies suddenly superhero  movies could be high art worthy of  awards and accolades all thanks to the  Caped Crusader and the Clown Prince of  Crime here was a film with one of the  greatest opening sequences of all time  it explored heavy concepts like what  people do when forced into terrible  circumstances and told the tragic story  of the rise and fall of Harvey Dent it  also featured the greatest 18-wheeler  flip of all time Heath Ledger won a  posthumous Oscar for his turn as the  Kaos loving Joker and all these years  later people still shudder when they  remember his freaky scars and his  terrifying magic trick it's a  performance for the ages  and thanks to ledger the Joker joined  the best cinematic villains alongside  Darth Vader and Hannibal Lecter with its  impressive acting pounding score  impeccable direction and intense action  The Dark Knight is the kind of superhero  movie that fans deserve and need  I'm just ahead of the curve check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite superhero movies are coming  soon subscribe to our YouTube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]
 

